          "prompt": "MANDATORY: ONE SINGLE HORIZONTAL ROW of exactly four separate orthographic views of the SAME object, left to right: 1 FRONT view; 2 LEFT side view (object turned so its front points to the LEFT edge of the image); 3 BACK view; 4 RIGHT side view (object turned so its front points to the RIGHT edge of the image). Same scale and same ground line in all four, wide empty gaps between the views, every view complete and not cropped. Plain flat light neutral grey background (#D6D6D6). No floor, no ground shadow, no text, no labels, no frames, no perspective, no extra objects. No fire, no smoke, no sparks, no lava, no glow halo: hot cracks, ember beds, flame tips and lantern glass are painted only as flat opaque bright orange-yellow colour areas.\n\nREFERENCE: the attached image is a crop of our approved scene concept. Redraw ONLY the basalt crag from it as a standalone game asset, keeping its shapes, proportions, materials and colours, simplified as described below; ignore everything else in the crop.\n\nSTYLE: stylized hand-painted 3D game environment asset: thick chunky silhouette that still reads as a solid black shape, broad clean faceted planes, two or three dominant colour blocks (dark violet-grey basalt, slightly lighter worn top planes), soft painted gradients, a few medium-size ornaments, sparse wear, soot-darkened edges. No photorealism, no micro-grain, no fine brick seams, no dense cracks, no tiny carvings, no harsh highlights. Anything at ground level is basalt, stone or cast iron; timber only high up on buildings.\n\nOBJECT (20m wide x 45m tall x 18m deep): A tall jagged basalt crag rising from the ground like a sheer cliff pillar, 45m tall, dark violet-grey rock in BIG smooth faceted planes: three or four huge vertical slabs leaning together, a broad foot spreading to 20m, a narrower broken top with two uneven peaks of different heights, one or two big horizontal ledges. Soft painted gradients, slightly lighter on the upper planes; no fine vertical striations, no small rubble. The silhouette is clearly different from every side. PROPORTIONS: FRONT and BACK views about 0.45 times as wide as tall; LEFT and RIGHT views about 0.4 times as wide as tall.",
